# Doom v1.9 shareware (id Software, 1995): installed from its own archive
# with its DEICE inside DOS, set up, and started to its first level.
# tests/keys.py turns this into the runners' --key options. The machine:
# the ASUS P/I-P55T2P4 (Pentium, 133 MHz) with its Award BIOS, 16 MB, IBM
# VGA, no sound card, the recompiler on, and a 30 MB hard disk on the
# board's own IDE port that the gate makes: FreeDOS, and the archive in
# C:\DMINST.
# No key for the BIOS: the core writes the CMOS the board's BIOS writes when
# it loads its defaults (waterbox/award-cmos.h), so it does not stop at "CMOS
# checksum error"; its hard disk type is "detect", and it finds the disk.
# FreeDOS's prompt by 2600.
2600 type cd dminst\n
2700 type install\n
# DEICE: drive C; the folder \DOOMS, as offered; create it, Y. It joins
# DOOMS_19.1 and .2 into DOOMS_19.EXE, the batch file runs it (it unpacks
# the game) and then SETUP.
3200 type c
3400 key Enter 4
3600 type y
# SETUP: keyboard only; no music; no sound effects (the machine has no sound
# card, the default each time); "Save parameters and launch DOOM".
5000 key Enter 4
5200 key Enter 4
5400 key Enter 4
5600 key Enter 4
# Doom's demo plays; Escape for the menu, New Game, the first episode
# (Knee-Deep in the Dead), the offered skill: E1M1 by frame 7600. Tab opens
# the map, which names the level at its foot: "E1M1: HANGAR".
7000 key Escape 4
7100 key Enter 4
7200 key Enter 4
7300 key Enter 4
7600 key Tab 4
